SUMMARY:[Hike - Beginner] Doube's Trestle Bridge\, 8-9kms/2hrs
DESCRIPTION:GTA Hiking & Stuff\nPlease join us for a speacial hike at Doub
 e's Trestle Bridge in Kawartha Lakes where we will hike the Trans Canada T
 rail and cross the Doube's Trestle Bridge!\n\nThe bridge has been closed d
 ue to a fire.\n\nThe hike takes place on an old railway line\, so this wou
 ld be considered a beginner hike as there will be no hills\, however\, we 
 are planning for between 8-9 kms total hiking.\n\nPlease wear sturdy hikin
 g boots and bring 1l of water. We will hike 8-9kms at a steady pace and wi
 ll stop for short breaks along the way.\n\nHike starts promptly at 10:05AM
 .\n\nThis is approx 1 hour away from Whitby by car. Please plan accordingl
 y.\n\nAs always\, this is a busy spot and you should car pool whenever pos
 sible.\n\n**LEGAL DISCLAIMER AND LIABILITY INFORMATION:**\n\nBy RSVP'ing a
 nd paying the event fee (if applicable)\, you are confirming that you have
  read\, understand and accept the following:\n\n1. **GTA Hiking Meetup is 
 a private group. Attending events is voluntary by you as a member. Partici
 pation in any activity with us is at your own risk.**\n2. **By joining thi
 s event as a member you agree to indemnify and hold harmless its organizer
 s\, co-organizers\, assistant organizers\, event hosts\, and other members
  from all claims or liability of every type (including court costs and leg
 al fees) for injury or death to any person or for damage to property\, los
 s of personal property or any other wrongful act arising out of or relatin
 g to your participation as a member.** This agreement applies to you and t
 o other persons (as your guests) who may accompany you in these endeavors.
 \n3. **You also agree to hold the organizers as well as other group member
 s harmless.** By participating voluntarily in the group\, you expressly wa
 ive any and all such claims against each and every other member in the gro
 up\, including without limitation any and all claims against the group org
 anizer\, co-organizers\, assistant organizers\, and event hosts.
